''Not to be confused with {{s|The Shop}}, a floor in [[Greed mode]].''

{{dlc|nr}}[[file:Locked Door.png]] {{dlc|r}}[[File:Shop door locked.png]][[File:Shop door.png]]

A {{r|Shop}} is a Special Room that sells various [[pickups]] and [[item]]s in exchange for {{E|Penny|text=Pennies}}. Shops require a {{E|Key}} to open, unless Isaac holds {{t|Store Key}} ({{dlc|r}} except on floor 1, where Shops are always initially unlocked), and appear in every [[Chapters|Chapter]] prior to {{s|Womb}} or including The Womb if Isaac holds {{t|Silver Dollar}}. {{dlc+|a}} Additionally, a single '''Shop''' always spawns adjacent to the {{s|???}} starting room.{{dlc-}}

Only one shop will ever appear on a floor at a time, even while under the effect of {{Cu|Labyrinth}}.

Shops have a chance of being replaced by a {{r|Mini-Boss Room}} containing {{E|Greed}} or {{E|Super Greed}} once entered, starting on the second floor of [[Chapter 2]]. Once both mini-bosses has been defeated in a Shop or {{r|Secret Room}}, they will not appear in either for the rest of the run.

* Greed will always spawn first, followed by Super Greed.
* {{dlc|nr}} If any mini-boss is encountered on the floor, including Greed/Super Greed in the secret room, Greed or Super Greed will not appear in the shop on that floor.
* {{t|Rib of Greed}} prevents both Greed and Super Greed from appearing in Shops while held.

=== {{dlc+|a}} Greed Mode ===
In [[Greed Mode]], Shops are twice as wide as usual and do not require a key to enter. They always contain a {{E|Key}}, a {{E|Red Heart}}, an item from the {{ip|Greed Shop|text=Greed Mode Shop item pool}}, an item from the {{ip|Greed Boss|text=Greed Mode Boss Room item pool}}, and two random pickups, trinkets, or items from the {{ip|Greed Treasure Room|text=Greed Mode Treasure Room item pool}}. The effect of {{i|Restock}} is always active inside of Shops in this mode ({{dlc|r}} prices will not increase continuously like they normally would when Isaac has Restock).

Shops will never be replaced by Greed or Super Greed in Greed Mode.

Layouts can be found [[Greed Mode#Layouts|here]].
{{dlc-}}

== Merchandise ==
* Shops can sell {{E|Red Heart}}s for {{pennies|3}}. They can also sell {{E|Soul Heart}}s, {{E|Bomb}}s, {{E|Key}}s, {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}}, [[Pills]], and [[Cards and Runes|Cards]] for {{pennies|5}} each.
** {{Dlc+|r}} Also: {{E|Grab Bag}}s for {{pennies|7}}.{{dlc-}}
* Shops can sell items for {{pennies|15}}, from among those found in the {{ip|Shop|text=Shop item pool}}.
** {{Dlc|r}} Certain active items are sold for {{pennies|10}}.
* Any purchasable item has a chance to be discounted, which will cut its price in half.
** Discounted items have red price tags instead of white price tags.
** If a discount leaves the price of an item at a number that is not an integer, items and {{e|Grab Bag|r}}s will round their price down while pickups will round their price up.
* {{i|Steam Sale}} will halve all prices in the Shop (and anywhere else items are bought for coins), {{dlc|nr}} including discounted ones.
** {{dlc|anr}} Two Steam Sales will make every item free, which can be combined with {{i|Restock|n}} to allow infinite purchasing power. This also holds true in Greed Mode.
<!--* {{dlc+|r}} There is a 20% chance for the shop to use a layout that contains a {{M|Shop Restock Machine}} if the Shop is level 1 or 2, and a 9% chance if the Shop is level 3 or 4.{{dlc-}}
** These layouts contain 1 less slot than their normal counterparts.-->

== Layouts ==
Shops start at level 0 and can be upgraded by donating Coins to the {{M|Donation Machine}}, which can be found in Shops and sometimes in {{r|Arcade}}s, {{r|Vault}}s, {{r|Black Market}}s, rare normal/special room layouts, and from pressing {{dlc|a}}[[Reward Plate]]s. Each level increases the number of items for sale and visually fills the walls of the Shop.

{{dlc|r}} Normal mode will always feature the highest unlocked level of Shop. In [[hard mode]], any level of shop that has been unlocked can appear. The room has 1/256 chance to be a rare shop (layouts 5, 6, 12, 13), then the weight determines which layout will be chosen. 

