== Notes ==
* The Shop can also be accessed through the usage of {{p|IX - The Hermit}}, a {{e|Golden Key}}, {{Cu|Maze}}, {{i|Dad's Key}}, bombing an adjacent {{r|Secret Room}} wall, or {{t|Store Key}}, without spending a Key.
* {{dlc|nr}} The Shop has a door that is identical to a {{r|Library}} as well as an identical symbol on the minimap. The Shop can never appear adjacent to the starting room (with the exception of the first floor), meaning that any one-key door that spawns adjacent to the starting room is a Library and not a Shop.
** {{t|Store Key}} will ''not'' open Library doors, which reveals which room the locked door will lead to.
* Using a {{p|Credit Card}} in the shop will make everything for sale free, spawning item pedestals and removing all listed prices.
** {{i|Restock}} only replenishes items that are bought for a listed price (including {{pennies|0}}); therefore, Credit Card negates the effect of Restock for that Shop.
* Holding {{t|Store Credit}} will reduce the price of all items to {{pennies|0}}. It will be consumed once an item is purchased. Unlike the {{p|Credit Card}}, {{i|Restock}} ''will'' restock the bought item.
** {{dlc+|anr}} If the {{t|Store Credit}} effect is gained through the effects of {{t|Error}}, it will not be consumed upon making a purchase; this can be combined with {{i|Restock}} to infinitely purchase items.{{dlc-}}
*** {{dlc|r}} Only 1 item can be bought for free without losing the trinket, even if Error is dropped and picked up again.
* {{i|Diplopia}} and {{p|Jera}} function as expected in Shops, generating free pickups/items.
* The [[Shopkeeper]] that spawns in the Shop can be bombed for potential rewards.
** {{E|Special Shopkeeper}} can replace the regular shopkeeper at a chance, which can drop better rewards.
* {{dlc|nr}} A total of 9 Shops maximum can be entered during a normal run — two in {{s|Basement}}/etc., two in {{s|Caves}}/etc., two in {{s|Depths}}/etc., two in {{s|Womb}}/etc. with the {{t|Silver Dollar}}, and one in {{s|???}}.
** {{dlc+|r}} This is increased to 10 if Isaac additionally holds {{t|Holy Crown}} or {{t|Wicked Crown}} in {{s|Cathedral}} or {{s|Sheol}} respectively, and Isaac can theoretically encounter many more Red Shops with {{i|Red Key}}.{{dlc-}}
** Multiple different shops can also be entered in one floor through resetting effects such as {{i|Forget Me Now}} or {{i|R Key}}.
* {{dlc+|r}} Items will increase in price the more bought with {{i|Restock}} until maxing out at 99 cents.{{dlc-}}

